026-02-13T02:16:49Z","updated_at":"2026-02-20T18:37:02Z","closed_at":"2026-02-16T16:24:54Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/116236","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116236","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116236.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116236.patch","merged_at":"2026-02-16T16:24:54Z"},"body":"Fixes #115369.\r\n\r\nSome compositors (e.g. COSMIC) can report *all* supported output modes, not just the current mode. This is valid, albeit deprecated, so let's add a check and ignore any non-current output events.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis meant that, on certain compositors, `screen_get_size` could return the wrong size, even really tiny stuff like 640x480. That said, even with this fix, the way we handle screens is still a hack and we should not depend on them in the long term.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.c